{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792421473,"nonce":"Y0FkqQStAugtrHfXgPybL+WMAmI=","title":"Web: after visiting every page and returning to Navigate, leaving it changes nothing and the page stops responding","message":"**Report**\nGo through each page, come back to Navigate, then try to switch to another page from it: the UI does not change and does not respond. The music goes on.\n\n**Not reproduced here**\nHarness: Chrome driven by CDP, the dashboard built from main with the block-compressed files, every page in dock order, back to Navigate, wait 1.5 s, click Media, look for the picture to change within 3 s; a counter on requestAnimationFrame and the collector's lines (ASH_GC_STATS) alongside.\n- headless, 1280 by 880: 6 rounds at 700 ms a page, 12 rounds at 200 ms and at 120 ms; the page changed in about 150 ms every time; live heap steady at 120-170 MB.\n- a real headed window at 2x, 1291 by 862, music playing, 8 rounds at 300 ms: the same.\nSo it is not the heap filling (that was the chargers map in the full layout, fixed in 4f998f1), and not the page switch itself. What would be different: the user's browser, display scaling and window size, and how long the page had been open before.\n\n**Tool**\nOpening the page with ?debug (log on the page) or ?watch (console) prints, each second, how many animation frames the page had, the longest gap, the time since the last, whether the page is hidden and the size of the program's shared memory. Two requestAnimationFrame loops run for the life of the page (the window shim's, which hands the program the browser's redraw, and the audio shim's), so a frozen page whose count goes on is the program stuck or waiting, a count of 0 is a browser not showing it, and a long gap is the main thread busy. With ?env=ASHUI_FRAME_STATS=1 the program says each second how many frames it drew and how many redraw waits ran out (it waits up to a second for the browser's redraw after a present, FRAME_WAIT_LIMIT), and ?env=ASH_GC_STATS=1 shows each collection (a full heap is origin=large-exhaustion, freed=0, again and again).\n\n**To ask**\nWhen it happens, with ?debug\u0026env=ASHUI_FRAME_STATS=1\u0026env=ASH_GC_STATS=1 on the address: do the [page] lines go on, do the [frames] lines, and what is the last [gc] line.","files":null}]}